  "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $z=4,$ we substitute $z=4$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $z$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+2)^{2} & =6(y+3) \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =2(y+3) \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (y+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a parabola in the $xy$-plane with the vertex at $(-2,-3).$",
